# Prompt Logging Convention -- Swaroop Formulation Industries

## Purpose

All AI prompts used during development MUST be logged for:
- **Reproducibility:** Any team member can recreate results.
- **Audit Trail:** Track what AI-generated content exists in the project.
- **Knowledge Transfer:** Document prompt engineering decisions.
- **Version Control:** Link prompts to specific code changes.

## Log File Location

```
documentation/prompts_log/YYYY-MM-DD_prompts.md
documentation/prompts_log/YYYY-MM-DD_prompts.tex
```

One file per day. Both `.md` and `.tex` versions must be maintained.

## Entry Format (Markdown)

```markdown
## Prompt Log Entry -- [Sequential ID]

- **Timestamp:** YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS
- **Level:** L1-Chatbot | L2-RAG | L3-Agentic | L4-Adaptive | L5-Platform | L6-Enterprise
- **Model:** <provider>/<model-name> (e.g., groq/llama-3-70b, openai/gpt-4o)
- **Category:** system-prompt | ingestion | agent-tool | scraper | report-gen | debug
- **Prompt:**
  ```
  [Full prompt text here]
  ```
- **Context:** [Why this prompt was needed, what problem it solves]
- **Outcome:** [What the model returned, whether it was accepted/modified]
- **Files Modified:** [List of files created or changed as a result]
- **Tokens Used:** [Approximate input/output token count if available]
```

## Entry Format (LaTeX)

```latex
\subsection{Prompt Log Entry -- [Sequential ID]}
\begin{description}
  \item[Timestamp] YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS
  \item[Level] L1-Chatbot
  \item[Model] groq/llama-3-70b
  \item[Category] system-prompt
  \item[Prompt] \begin{lstlisting}
    [Full prompt text]
  \end{lstlisting}
  \item[Context] Why this prompt was needed.
  \item[Outcome] What the model returned.
  \item[Files Modified] src/utils/system-prompt.ts
  \item[Tokens Used] ~500 input / ~200 output
\end{description}
```

## Categories

| Category | Description |
|---|---|
| `system-prompt` | System prompts for chatbot or agents |
| `ingestion` | Prompts used during document ingestion or chunking decisions |
| `agent-tool` | Prompts for agent tool descriptions or routing |
| `scraper` | Prompts used to parse or clean scraped data |
| `report-gen` | Prompts for auto-generating reports or documents |
| `debug` | Prompts used to debug issues |
| `translation` | Prompts for language translation |
| `content` | Prompts for generating marketing/social content |

## Rules

1. Log EVERY prompt that produces code or content committed to the repository.
2. Include the full prompt text -- do not summarize or truncate.
3. If a prompt is iterated multiple times, log each iteration as a separate entry.
4. Link each entry to the git commit that contains the resulting changes.
5. At the end of each week, review the log for patterns and add a summary section.
